        "original_id": "451a704e-7237-5a0e-bb8b-eb5904a5086b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Songs/Anthems: Ich hab' mich ergeben, Deutschlandlied, Patriots of Micronesia, Auferstanden aus Ruinen\n- Places/States: Germany, West Germany, East Germany, Micronesia\n\nFacts:\n- The Deutschlandlied has been the national anthem of Germany since 1922, except in East Germany from 1949 to 1990, when Auferstanden aus Ruinen was East Germany's anthem.\n- Ich hab' mich ergeben was one of the unofficial national anthems of West Germany between 1949 and 1952.\n- The Deutschlandlied was officially reinstated in West Germany in 1952.\n- Patriots of Micronesia uses the melody of the German student song Ich hab' mich ergeben.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "87b07cec-394f-52e1-8515-a00ff71f98ad",
        "text": "Page: Ich hab' mich ergeben. Sentence: It was one of the unofficial national anthems of West Germany between 1949 and 1952 when the Deutschlandlied was officially reinstalled.\nPage: Deutschlandlied. Sentence: The \"Deutschlandlied \" (English: \"Song of Germany\", ] ; also known as \"Das Lied der Deutschen \" or \"The Song of the Germans\"), or part of it, has been the national anthem of Germany since 1922, except in East Germany, whose anthem was \"Auferstanden aus Ruinen\" (\"Risen from Ruins\") from 1949 to 1990.\nPage: Patriots of Micronesia. Sentence: The melody is that of the German student song \"Ich hab' mich ergeben\" (which was also one of the unofficial anthems of West Germany between 1949 and 1952).",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
      {
